IMPORT prelude

-- Legislation Act 2003 (Commonwealth), Chapter 1 Part 2, sections 12 to 14: commencement, construction and incorporation of instruments.
-- Text: C2004A01224.txt, compilation C2019C00084; it is not the authorised text.
-- The answers are MAYBE BOOLEAN in the same way as in lga-register.l4: JUST TRUE (the text says yes), JUST FALSE (the text says no), NOTHING (the text does not say).
-- The day on which an instrument commences is computed in lga-time.l4 (s 12(1)(a)).

§ `Section 12: commencement of legislative instruments and notifiable instruments`

-- "so far as the instrument provides otherwise": where the instrument has its own commencement provision, paragraph (b) governs that matter and (a) does not.
-- src:241 | (1) A legislative instrument or a notifiable instrument commences:
-- src:242 | (a) at the start of the day after the day the instrument is registered; or
-- src:243 | (b) so far as the instrument provides otherwise—in accordance with such provision.
-- src:244 | Note: The instrument may provide for its commencement by enabling a commencement instrument to be made: see subsection (5).
@ref s 12(1) (src:241-244)
GIVEN `it is a legislative instrument or a notifiable instrument` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the instrument provides otherwise for its commencement` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 12(1)(a): the instrument commences at the start of the day after the day it is registered` MEANS
    IF `it is a legislative instrument or a notifiable instrument`
    THEN (IF `the instrument provides otherwise for its commencement` THEN JUST FALSE ELSE JUST TRUE)
    ELSE NOTHING

@ref s 12(1)(b) (src:243-243)
GIVEN `it is a legislative instrument or a notifiable instrument` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the instrument provides otherwise for its commencement` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 12(1)(b): the instrument commences in accordance with its own commencement provision` MEANS
    IF `it is a legislative instrument or a notifiable instrument`
    THEN (IF `the instrument provides otherwise for its commencement` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE)
    ELSE NOTHING

-- jural: power of the rule-maker | liability of anyone the instrument governs
-- src:246 | (1A) Despite any principle or rule of common law, a legislative instrument or notifiable instrument may provide that the instrument, or a provision of the instrument, commences before the instrument is registered.
-- src:247 | Note: The effect of this subsection is to allow legislative and notifiable instruments to commence retrospectively (subject to subsection (2)). This subsection is subject to a contrary provision (see subsection (4)).
@ref s 12(1A) (src:246-247)
GIVEN `it is a legislative instrument or a notifiable instrument` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 12(1A): the instrument, or a provision of it, may provide that it commences before the instrument is registered` MEANS
    IF `it is a legislative instrument or a notifiable instrument` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- jural: immunity of a person other than the Commonwealth or an authority of the Commonwealth | disability of the rule-maker to bind that person to the extent of the result
-- The Commonwealth and its authorities are outside the words of (2), so the answer for them is NOTHING.
-- src:249 | (2) However, if a legislative instrument or notifiable instrument, or a provision of such an instrument, commences before the instrument is registered, the instrument or provision does not apply in relation to a person (other than the Commonwealth or an authority of the Commonwealth) to the extent that as a result of that commencement:
-- src:250 | (a) the person’s rights as at the time the instrument is registered would be affected so as to disadvantage the person; or
-- src:251 | (b) liabilities would be imposed on the person in respect of anything done or omitted to be done before the instrument is registered.
@ref s 12(2) (src:249-251)
GIVEN `the instrument, or the provision, commences before the instrument is registered` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is the Commonwealth or an authority of the Commonwealth` IS A BOOLEAN
      `as a result of that commencement the person's rights as at the time the instrument is registered would be affected so as to disadvantage the person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `as a result of that commencement liabilities would be imposed on the person in respect of anything done or omitted to be done before the instrument is registered` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 12(2): the instrument or provision does not apply in relation to the person to the extent of that result` MEANS
    IF NOT `the instrument, or the provision, commences before the instrument is registered`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE
        IF `the person is the Commonwealth or an authority of the Commonwealth`
        THEN NOTHING
        ELSE
            IF `as a result of that commencement the person's rights as at the time the instrument is registered would be affected so as to disadvantage the person`
               OR `as a result of that commencement liabilities would be imposed on the person in respect of anything done or omitted to be done before the instrument is registered`
            THEN JUST TRUE
            ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:253 | (4) The effect of subsection (1A) or (2) in relation to an instrument is subject to any contrary provision in an Act.
@ref s 12(4) (src:253-253)
GIVEN `an Act has a contrary provision` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 12(4): the effect of subsection (1A) or (2) is displaced by the contrary provision in the Act` MEANS
    IF `an Act has a contrary provision` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- jural: power of the rule-maker | liability of the commencement of the instrument
-- src:255 | (5) Without limiting paragraph (1)(b), for the purposes of that paragraph, a legislative instrument or notifiable instrument may authorise the making of a commencement instrument in relation to the legislative instrument or notifiable instrument.
@ref s 12(5) (src:255-255)
GIVEN `it is a legislative instrument or a notifiable instrument` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 12(5): the instrument may authorise the making of a commencement instrument in relation to it` MEANS
    IF `it is a legislative instrument or a notifiable instrument` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

§ `Section 13: construction of legislative instruments and notifiable instruments`

-- "unless the contrary intention appears": with a contrary intention the answer is JUST FALSE; without a conferred power the section does not speak, so NOTHING.
-- src:257 | (1) If enabling legislation confers on a person the power to make a legislative instrument or notifiable instrument, then, unless the contrary intention appears:
-- src:258 | (a) the Acts Interpretation Act 1901 applies to any instrument so made as if it were an Act and as if each provision of the instrument were a section of an Act; and
-- src:259 | (b) expressions used in any instrument so made have the same meaning as in the enabling legislation as in force from time to time; and
-- src:260 | (c) any instrument so made is to be read and construed subject to the enabling legislation as in force from time to time, and so as not to exceed the power of the person to make the instrument.
@ref s 13(1) (src:257-260)
GIVEN `enabling legislation confers on a person the power to make the legislative instrument or notifiable instrument` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the contrary intention appears` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 13(1)(a): the Acts Interpretation Act 1901 applies to the instrument as if it were an Act and each provision were a section` MEANS
    IF `enabling legislation confers on a person the power to make the legislative instrument or notifiable instrument`
    THEN (IF `the contrary intention appears` THEN JUST FALSE ELSE JUST TRUE)
    ELSE NOTHING

@ref s 13(1)(b) (src:259-259)
GIVEN `enabling legislation confers on a person the power to make the legislative instrument or notifiable instrument` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the contrary intention appears` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 13(1)(b): expressions in the instrument have the same meaning as in the enabling legislation as in force from time to time` MEANS
    IF `enabling legislation confers on a person the power to make the legislative instrument or notifiable instrument`
    THEN (IF `the contrary intention appears` THEN JUST FALSE ELSE JUST TRUE)
    ELSE NOTHING

@ref s 13(1)(c) (src:260-260)
GIVEN `enabling legislation confers on a person the power to make the legislative instrument or notifiable instrument` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the contrary intention appears` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 13(1)(c): the instrument is to be read and construed subject to the enabling legislation and so as not to exceed the power` MEANS
    IF `enabling legislation confers on a person the power to make the legislative instrument or notifiable instrument`
    THEN (IF `the contrary intention appears` THEN JUST FALSE ELSE JUST TRUE)
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:261 | (2) If the making of a legislative instrument or notifiable instrument would, apart from this subsection, be construed as being in excess of the power to make the instrument, it is to be taken to be a valid instrument to the extent to which it is not in excess of that power.
@ref s 13(2) (src:261-261)
GIVEN `the making of the instrument would, apart from this subsection, be construed as being in excess of the power to make it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 13(2): the instrument stands to the extent to which it is not in excess of that power` MEANS
    IF `the making of the instrument would, apart from this subsection, be construed as being in excess of the power to make it` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE

-- jural: privilege of the person exercising the power | no-right of anyone to require each matter to be named separately
-- src:262 | (3) If enabling legislation confers on a person the power to make a legislative instrument or notifiable instrument:
-- src:263 | (a) specifying, declaring or prescribing a matter; or
-- src:264 | (b) doing anything in relation to a matter;
-- src:265 | then, in exercising the power, the person may identify the matter by referring to a class or classes of matters.
@ref s 13(3) (src:262-265)
GIVEN `enabling legislation confers on a person the power to make a legislative instrument or notifiable instrument` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the power is to specify, declare or prescribe a matter, or to do anything in relation to a matter` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 13(3): in exercising the power the person may identify the matter by referring to a class or classes of matters` MEANS
    IF `enabling legislation confers on a person the power to make a legislative instrument or notifiable instrument`
       AND `the power is to specify, declare or prescribe a matter, or to do anything in relation to a matter`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE

DECLARE `Kind of subject for section 13(4)` IS ONE OF
    thing
    person
    animal
    `something else`

-- "matter includes thing, person and animal": the three named are matters; anything else is not covered.
-- src:266 | (4) For the purposes of subsection (3), matter includes thing, person and animal.
@ref s 13(4) (src:266-266)
GIVEN `the kind` IS A `Kind of subject for section 13(4)`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 13(4): the subject is a matter` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the kind`
    WHEN thing THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN person THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN animal THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `something else` THEN NOTHING

-- src:267 | (5) The amendment of a legislative instrument or notifiable instrument by an Act does not prevent the instrument, as so amended, from being amended or repealed by a person who is currently authorised under the enabling legislation for the instrument to make instruments of the same kind.
-- src:268 | Note: This section has a parallel, in relation to instruments other than legislative instruments or notifiable instruments, in subsection 33(3AB) and section 46 of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901.
@ref s 13(5) (src:267-268)
GIVEN `the instrument has been amended by an Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is currently authorised under the enabling legislation to make instruments of the same kind` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 13(5): the amendment by an Act prevents the instrument from being amended or repealed by the person` MEANS
    IF `the instrument has been amended by an Act` AND `the person is currently authorised under the enabling legislation to make instruments of the same kind` THEN JUST FALSE ELSE NOTHING

§ `Section 14: prescribing matters by reference to other instruments`

DECLARE `Where the matter comes from` IS ONE OF
    `the provisions of an Act`
    `the provisions of a legislative instrument covered by subsection (3)`
    `the provisions of rules of court`
    `any other instrument or writing`

DECLARE `When the matter is taken` IS ONE OF
    `as in force at the time the instrument commences`
    `as in force or existing at a time before the instrument commences`
    `as in force at a particular time after the instrument commences`
    `as in force from time to time`

-- src:279 | (3) The following legislative instruments are covered by this subsection:
-- src:280 | (a) disallowable legislative instruments;
-- src:281 | (b) legislative instruments that were disallowable under the Acts Interpretation Act 1901 or any other Act at any time before 1 January 2005.
-- src:282 | Note: The substantive provisions of this Act commenced on 1 January 2005.
@ref s 14(3) (src:279-282)
GIVEN `it is a disallowable legislative instrument` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it was disallowable under the Acts Interpretation Act 1901 or any other Act at any time before 1 January 2005` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 14(3): the legislative instrument is covered by this subsection` MEANS
    `it is a disallowable legislative instrument`
    OR `it was disallowable under the Acts Interpretation Act 1901 or any other Act at any time before 1 January 2005`

-- jural: power of the rule-maker | liability of anyone bound by the instrument
-- Paragraph (a): an Act, a covered legislative instrument or rules of court, as in force at a particular time or from time to time.
-- src:270 | (1) If enabling legislation authorises or requires provision to be made in relation to any matter by a legislative instrument or notifiable instrument, the instrument may, unless the contrary intention appears, make provision in relation to that matter:
-- src:271 | (a) by applying, adopting or incorporating, with or without modification, any of the following, as in force at a particular time or as in force from time to time:
-- src:272 | (i) the provisions of an Act;
-- src:273 | (ii) the provisions of a legislative instrument covered by subsection (3);
-- src:274 | (iii) the provisions of rules of court; or
-- src:275 | (b) subject to subsection (2), by applying, adopting or incorporating, with or without modification, any matter contained in any other instrument or writing as in force or existing at:
-- src:276 | (i) the time the first-mentioned instrument commences; or
-- src:277 | (ii) a time before the first-mentioned instrument commences (whether or not the other instrument is still in force, or the other writing still exists, at the time the first-mentioned instrument commences).
@ref s 14(1) (src:270-277)
GIVEN `enabling legislation authorises or requires provision to be made in relation to the matter by a legislative instrument or notifiable instrument` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the contrary intention appears` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the source` IS A `Where the matter comes from`
      `the time` IS A `When the matter is taken`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 14(1): the instrument may make provision in relation to the matter by applying, adopting or incorporating it` MEANS
    IF NOT `enabling legislation authorises or requires provision to be made in relation to the matter by a legislative instrument or notifiable instrument`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE
        IF `the contrary intention appears`
        THEN JUST FALSE
        ELSE
            CONSIDER `the source`
            WHEN `the provisions of an Act` THEN JUST TRUE
            WHEN `the provisions of a legislative instrument covered by subsection (3)` THEN JUST TRUE
            WHEN `the provisions of rules of court` THEN JUST TRUE
            WHEN `any other instrument or writing` THEN
                CONSIDER `the time`
                WHEN `as in force at the time the instrument commences` THEN JUST TRUE
                WHEN `as in force or existing at a time before the instrument commences` THEN JUST TRUE
                WHEN `as in force at a particular time after the instrument commences` THEN NOTHING
                WHEN `as in force from time to time` THEN NOTHING

-- jural: immunity of anyone bound by the instrument | disability of the rule-maker
-- Subsection (2): "may not ... as in force or existing from time to time", unless the contrary intention appears.
-- src:278 | (2) Unless the contrary intention appears, the legislative instrument or notifiable instrument may not make provision in relation to a matter by applying, adopting or incorporating any matter contained in an instrument or other writing as in force or existing from time to time.
@ref s 14(2) (src:278-278)
GIVEN `the contrary intention appears` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the source` IS A `Where the matter comes from`
      `the time` IS A `When the matter is taken`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 14(2): the instrument may not make provision by applying, adopting or incorporating the matter as in force or existing from time to time` MEANS
    IF `the contrary intention appears` THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE
        CONSIDER `the source`
        WHEN `any other instrument or writing` THEN
            CONSIDER `the time`
            WHEN `as in force from time to time` THEN JUST TRUE
            WHEN `as in force at the time the instrument commences` THEN NOTHING
            WHEN `as in force or existing at a time before the instrument commences` THEN NOTHING
            WHEN `as in force at a particular time after the instrument commences` THEN NOTHING
        WHEN `the provisions of an Act` THEN NOTHING
        WHEN `the provisions of a legislative instrument covered by subsection (3)` THEN NOTHING
        WHEN `the provisions of rules of court` THEN NOTHING

-- src:284 | (4) If a legislative instrument or notifiable instrument provides for a form to be used, this section does not apply in relation to the form.
-- src:285 | Note: This section has a parallel, in relation to instruments that are not legislative instruments, in section 46AA of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901.
@ref s 14(4) (src:284-285)
GIVEN `the legislative instrument or notifiable instrument provides for a form to be used` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 14(4): section 14 applies in relation to the form` MEANS
    IF `the legislative instrument or notifiable instrument provides for a form to be used` THEN JUST FALSE ELSE NOTHING
